{
    "background_story": "Koa was a young Hawaiian navigator who lived in the 15th century. Growing up on the island of Oahu, he was fascinated by the ancient art of wayfinding, passed down through generations of his family. Koa spent years studying the movements of the stars, winds, and currents, learning to read the subtle signs of nature that guided sailors across the vast Pacific. As a skilled wayfinder, Koa led numerous expeditions to distant islands, discovering new lands and establishing trade routes. His expertise and bravery earned him the respect of his people, and he became known as the greatest navigator of his time. Koa's knowledge of the way helped his people thrive, connecting them to the world beyond their shores and forging a lasting legacy.",
